@startuml proj-service-c4-context
' C4 Context — PROJ (Projetos) within the Cordelê modular monolith
title Cordelê — PROJ (Projetos) — System Context

actor "Coordenador(a) Editorial" as Editor
actor "Dev team (IMP/COMP/PUB)" as Dev

rectangle "BFF (NestJS)\nsingle gateway — TECH-003" as BFF
rectangle "PROJ context\n(proj-service)\nproject identity + lifecycle status" as PROJ

rectangle "IMP context\n(manuscritos)" as IMP
rectangle "COMP context\n(metadados/layout)" as COMP
rectangle "PUB context\n(publicacoes/ePub)" as PUB
database "PostgreSQL 16\nschema-per-tenant" as PG
cloud "Object storage\n(ePub / binaries)" as OBJ

Editor --> BFF : create / library (T02) / detail / history (T08) / reopen / delete
BFF --> PROJ : /api/proj (OAuth2 JWT, EmpresaContext)

IMP --> PROJ : advanceTo(em_composicao) ; create/lookup (in-process)
PUB --> PROJ : advanceTo(publicado|com_erros) (in-process)

PROJ --> IMP : ManuscriptSummaryPort ; ManuscriptErasurePort (in-process)
PROJ --> COMP : ProjectMetadataPort ; CompositionErasurePort (in-process)
PROJ --> PUB : PublicationHistoryPort (+ signed URL) ; PublicationErasurePort (in-process)

PROJ --> PG : projeto_editorial + projeto_status_historico (tenant schema)
Editor ..> OBJ : downloads ePub via signed URL (never proxied by PROJ)
PUB --> OBJ : owns/signs ePub artifacts

note right of PROJ
  No broker, no AI, no hub (ai.hasAi=false,
  messaging.enabled=false). All cross-context
  calls are in-process ports (ADR-001/ADR-002).
end note
@enduml
